      "id": 1,
      "text": "Guntown was founded on April 13, 1866, and officially incorporated as the Town of Guntown on February 16, 1867.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guntown%2C_Mississippi",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name honors Virginia loyalist émigré James G. Gunn, who settled in the area during the 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guntown%2C_Mississippi",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During the Civil War, U.S. Cavalry officers described Guntown as a small village on the Mobile & Ohio road.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guntown%2C_Mississippi",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Guntown sits in the northern part of the Tupelo micropolitan area, linking it to the regional economy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
